WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:06.540
Here's a short venture into the failed ideas
that are floating around to fight Corona virus.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.120
Louisiana is a state that is really suffering
with coronavirus.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:14.429
Louisiana has the fourth most cases per capita.

00:00:14.429 --> 00:00:18.030
Louisiana has the seventh most deaths per
capita.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:23.180
But most importantly, the disease is quickly
returning to Louisiana, where from early June

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.680
through yesterday, cases have gone higher
and higher.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.720
Louisiana has more people actively infected
today than at any previous point during the

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.730
pandemic.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.730
So what is Louisiana Governor John Bel Edwards
do?

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:42.530
Well, he obviously calls for three days of
prayer and fasting.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:46.150
Now, Belle Edwards is a Democrat, by the way.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:51.930
He says pastors reached out to him and said,
you know, you should maybe support fasting

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.580
and prayer to deal with the virus.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.690
So he's going to be calling for it statewide.

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:58.450
Take a look at this.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:06.100
I do want to let you all know that that every
couple, three weeks I have a the opportunity

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:12.770
to have a conference call with hundreds of
pastors across the state of Louisiana.

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:17.630
And last week, we had such a call and received
a request.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:21.170
And I'm happy to honor today.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:26.609
And and it's I know it's a little bit unusual,
but but I think it's it's something that it's

00:01:26.609 --> 00:01:31.459
important, at least for me and those people
on the call and many other Louisianans.

00:01:31.459 --> 00:01:36.189
So I'm going to call for three days of fasting
and prayer for our state for July 20th through

00:01:36.189 --> 00:01:37.609
the 22nd.

00:01:37.609 --> 00:01:41.630
So that's the 20th to 21st, the 22nd.

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:48.409
This will be the spiritual diet and exercise
that I, as a Catholic Christian believes very

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:49.829
important anyway.

00:01:49.829 --> 00:01:56.869
So we'll be doing lunch, fasting for those
three days and certainly praying as well,

00:01:56.869 --> 00:01:57.869
praying for the

00:01:57.869 --> 00:02:02.579
people of Louisiana, praying for those who
are sick, praying for those who care for those

00:02:02.579 --> 00:02:08.739
who are sick, and certainly praying for the
families of those who have passed on.

00:02:08.739 --> 00:02:12.590
You know, he he is right when he says it's
unusual.

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:17.819
That started yesterday, by the way, July 20th,
the fasting and prayer supposed to be yesterday,

00:02:17.819 --> 00:02:18.819
today and tomorrow.

00:02:18.819 --> 00:02:24.769
Now, as he Matmata said, Hemant Hemant meant
said in a blog post, what Bel Edwards does

00:02:24.769 --> 00:02:28.079
in his spare time is really his business.

00:02:28.079 --> 00:02:34.500
But what pastors want him to do should be
irrelevant from the standpoint of public announcements

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.660
as the secular governor of the state of Louisiana.

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.510
Now, I don't mean personally a religious.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:46.370
I mean that the governorship itself should
be secular, separated from religion.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:51.030
There is no reason to tell people of the state
to do a religious ritual to fight a virus.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.640
We know what he should be calling for.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:53.829
We know what needs to be done.

00:02:53.829 --> 00:02:57.150
Everybody should be wearing a mask, which
he did say in his defense.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.450
No large group gatherings

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.110
mostly stay home, certainly no indoor dining.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:04.019
We know what to do.

00:03:04.019 --> 00:03:05.170
And the mask part.

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:09.120
He did say, but he's calling for prayer and
fasting.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.680
And, you know, some people are defending this
by saying he said this is it.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:15.629
Non-denominational, right.

00:03:15.629 --> 00:03:18.890
Skip lunch and and pray regardless of.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:19.989
Of your denomination.

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:22.680
What about people who aren't religious?

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:29.700
This is still a government actor who is supposed
to be separate from the church establishing

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:30.950
a religious act.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:35.700
I mean, prayer is a religious act over non
religion.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.030
And it's another example of of this.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:40.019
You know, we've tried nothing and we're out
of ideas.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.989
I mean, he's already going to prayer and fasting.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.489
And it's a Democratic governor, not a Republican.

00:03:45.489 --> 00:03:48.280
This is not about political party for me.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:50.330
Mostly this type of stuff is in the Republican
Party.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.980
But here's an example of it from the Democratic
side.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.799
This is certainly a conservative Democrat.

00:03:54.799 --> 00:03:55.940
Don't be confused.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.260
But still, this is a Democrat.

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:00.299
And it reminds me of the situation in Mississippi.

00:04:00.299 --> 00:04:02.190
Actually, we've talked about Mississippi.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:07.790
Mississippi is tragically suffering and has
been for decades in the United States.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:10.080
And yet they're talking and doing nonsense.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.739
In Mississippi, it was.

00:04:11.739 --> 00:04:18.209
Well, how can we block black voters from from
voting or how can we make sure that more real

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:23.370
Mississippians register because the blacks
are really registering to vote.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:28.210
Meanwhile, Mississippi is almost dead last
or dead last in health care, education, et

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.680
cetera, et cetera.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:36.390
Louisiana is one of the most ravaged states
by most indicators.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:38.840
Louisiana's forty fifth in health care.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.700
Forty eighth in education.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.740
Forty ninth in economic growth.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.600
Forty eighth in infrastructure.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.240
Fiftieth in dealing with climate change.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.850
It's a disaster in Louisiana.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.240
And then you look over and how are they dealing

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.240
with Corona virus?

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:56.050
Well, the governor suggests skipping lunch
and praying.

00:04:56.050 --> 00:05:02.570
Now, someone wrote to me something that that
is interesting, which is could this be indirectly

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:03.570
brilliant?

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:11.160
In other words, Bel Edwards could be appealing
to religiosity by saying fast during lunch.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:17.700
Lunch is when a lot of folks go out, especially
if they're working, maybe by saying skip lunch.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:21.700
He's keeping people out of restaurants and
it's actually going to stop the spread.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:22.700
I don't know.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.150
It's an interesting question.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:29.590
It's certainly the most charitable interpretation
of fast and pray to stop the virus.

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:32.280
But that's not really what what this is about.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:38.680
This is not about reverse engineering, some
way in which a call for fasting and prayer

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:42.480
might connect to better health outcomes with
Corona virus.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.900
This is a governor, a public elected official.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:50.600
He has no place suggesting religious prayer
and fasting on the say

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:55.810
so of Christian pastors as a solution for
a public health crisis.

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:59.580
And again, look at how poorly things are going
in Louisiana.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.710
We have to ask whether these things are connected.

